  "premise_review": [
    "SpectralBoundaryData carries real Boundary/element/Place→Option data but aligned is an independently chosen Prop with no relation to those fields. SpectralBoundaryAlignment adds its proof, exact modeled zeroData map, optional strong/Tate/homotopy packages and source label. None defines an analytic spectrum or actual zeros of a function.",
    "The separate SpectralBoundaryCriticalLineBridge is genuine supplied dependent evidence: aligned→∀z,LiesOnCriticalLine(zeroData z). Keep its entire original A/S/Z dependency and source notice. The source correctly needs a separately supplied bridge B; no proof constructs B.",
    "The two critical-line theorems preserve all S/Z/A/B/z premises, actual target predicate and original calls unchanged. The target reduces under the fully read original providers to the supplied realPart equaling spectralPivot=1/2; modeled Z can be empty and nontrivial is an independent unproved Prop.",
    "The theorem named does_not_force_critical_line_alone proves only True by trivial under an unused _A. Its actual proof is acknowledged; no logical non-implication/independence or absence theorem is inferred from the name.",
    "The complete local mixed own-provider schema and all four genuine theorem bodies stay archived. Extracting a standalone bridge would require the newly local A schema via a new self-import or copying/narrowing the independent aligned field; neither is introduced.",
    "Full exact zero/critical-line/pivot/absolute-deviation/typed-zero contexts and optional contract providers were read. Root Core/DualPivot and ZeroTypology path matches remain contextual; no canonical path aliases or replacement providers are activated. All source docs and optional fields remain exact."
